  "_mu_p_audit_note": "mu_substrate_tension_audit_100dps is listed PHYSICAL, alone. This is NOT the bulk migration (qou-1c4y) and does not depend on it. The producer's SUBJECT is the difference between the two pins: it computes the muon leg itself by inverting CODATA m_mu/m_e and takes the OTHER leg from Q_50_DIGIT_STR. Listed ideal_muon, that leg was muon too, so it differenced muon against muon and reported the literal-vs-inversion residual (0.075 ppb) as the substrate tension (11.61 ppb) -- understating its own subject 155x. A producer needing BOTH pins cannot be served by a per-process override that supplies one; it is miscategorised on its own terms. Since PR #5049 landed a run-time assertion that the proton leg is proton, leaving it here also makes the audit exit 1 rather than run.",
